# Packaging whitelist (`build.json` → `files`)

`build.json` `files` is an **explicit allowlist**. Root-level modules required by `main.js` (or other packaged files) are **not** auto-included.

## When this applies

- Adding a new root file such as `foo-store.js`, `foo-lib.js`
- Changing `main.js` / `preload.js` to `require("./something.js")`
- Splitting logic out of an existing root module into a new file

## Required checklist

1. Create / edit the source file as usual.
2. Add the exact path to `build.json` → `files` (same style as `db-store.js`, `assets-store.js`, `media-gen-global-lock.js`).
3. Run `scripts\agent-rebuild.cmd` so `dist\win-unpacked` picks it up.
4. If you see `Cannot find module './xxx.js'` only in the packaged app (not `electron .`), the file is almost always missing from this whitelist.

## Do not

- Assume "it's next to main.js so packaging will include it"
- Only update `dist/` by hand — afterPack / compile regenerates from the whitelist
